=== HOW TO READ THIS ===
These are statements about the effects given the data, not about hypothetical
repetitions of the experiment. A probability near 50% means the data are
silent on the question; one near 100% means they settle it. They are read
alongside the frequentist results, not instead of them: both come from the
same model and the same data, so they cannot disagree about the evidence,
only about how it is phrased.
